exports[`renderMarkdown > renders nested workflows grouped by severity, errors first 1`] = `
"## flowpact report

<sub>flowpact v0.0.0-test · config schema v1 · contract schema v1 · report schema v1 · 7 ms</sub>

❌ **4 errors** · 7 warnings · 2 info

| Errors | Warnings | Info | Suppressed | Workflows | Actions | Jobs | Matrix combinations |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 4 | 7 | 2 | 0 | 4 | 0 | 7 | 0 |

### ❌ Errors (4)

**[\`FP101\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp101) missing-required-input** · \`.github/workflows/build.yml:29:11\`

jobs.package calls .github/workflows/package.yml without required input "channel"

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** For reusable workflows GitHub fails the run when a required input is missing — even if the input also has a \`default\`, which is then never used. For composite actions \`required\` is not enforced at all: the step silently runs with an empty string (or the default), which is how test variants get skipped unnoticed.

**Fix:** Add \`channel: <value>\` under \`with:\` of jobs.package.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:21:11\` — jobs.build calls .github/workflows/build.yml
- \`.github/workflows/package.yml:11:7\` — "channel" is declared required here

</details>

**[\`FP201\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp201) missing-required-secret** · \`.github/workflows/build.yml:29:11\`

jobs.package calls .github/workflows/package.yml without required secret "signing-key"

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** GitHub fails the run when a required secret is not passed — but only when that call path actually executes.

**Fix:** Pass the secret under \`secrets:\`, or use \`secrets: inherit\` if the callee should see all repository secrets.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:21:11\` — jobs.build calls .github/workflows/build.yml
- \`.github/workflows/package.yml:17:7\` — declared required here

</details>

**[\`FP301\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp301) undefined-output-ref** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:33:73\`

jobs.build has no output "image-digest"

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Undefined outputs evaluate to an empty string. Downstream jobs then run with missing versions, tags or flags.

**Fix:** Fix the output name, declare the output on the job/workflow/action, or reference the right job or step. In a composite action, a step writing to \`$GITHUB_OUTPUT\` sets its own output, not the action's: give the step an \`id\` and map the output under the action's \`outputs:\` (\`value: \${{ steps.<id>.outputs.<name> }}\`).

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/build.yml:3:3\` — .github/workflows/build.yml declares outputs: artifact-url

</details>

**[\`FP302\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp302) output-ref-without-needs** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:39:33\`

jobs.notify reads needs.build, which is empty here: "build" is not under needs, and only the job's \`if:\` sees jobs it depends on indirectly

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** The \`needs\` context contains the jobs listed under \`needs:\`. Only the job's own \`if:\` also sees the jobs it depends on indirectly (through one of its needs); in steps, \`env\`, \`with:\`, \`name\` and the matrix their values are empty. A job that does not depend on \`<job>\` at all may also run before it.

**Fix:** Add "build" to jobs.notify.needs.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:36:12\` — needs: deploy

</details>

### ⚠️ Warnings (7)

**[\`FP104\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp104) unused-input** · \`.github/workflows/build.yml:11:7\`

Input "verbose" of .github/workflows/build.yml is never read (yet 1 caller passes it)

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Dead inputs accumulate in large interfaces: callers keep computing and passing values that go nowhere, and readers assume a knob works when it does not.

**Fix:** Remove the input (and the callers’ bindings), or wire it to where it was meant to be used.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:25:7\` — passed here

</details>

**[\`FP303\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp303) unused-output** · \`.github/workflows/build.yml:22:7\`

Output "checksum" of jobs.compile is never read

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Unused outputs suggest a broken hand-off: either the consumer reads a different name, or the output is dead code.

**Fix:** Remove the output, or make the intended consumer read it.

</details>

**[\`FP304\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp304) step-output-never-written** · \`.github/workflows/build.yml:22:21\`

Step "sum" never writes output "sha" (it writes sha256) — did you mean "sha256"?

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** The read evaluates to an empty string. This is typically a typo in the \`echo "name=value" >> $GITHUB_OUTPUT\` line.

**Fix:** Write the output in the step (\`echo "<name>=<value>" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"\`) or read the name it actually writes.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/build.yml:25:14\` — outputs are written here

</details>

**[\`FP203\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp203) unused-secret** · \`.github/workflows/package.yml:17:7\`

Secret "signing-key" of .github/workflows/package.yml is never read

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Every caller must still wire the secret, widening its exposure for nothing.

**Fix:** Remove the declaration and the callers’ \`secrets:\` bindings, or use the secret where intended.

</details>

**[\`FP104\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp104) unused-input** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:15:7\`

Input "legacy-flag" of .github/workflows/pipeline.yml is never read

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Dead inputs accumulate in large interfaces: callers keep computing and passing values that go nowhere, and readers assume a knob works when it does not.

**Fix:** Remove the input (and the callers’ bindings), or wire it to where it was meant to be used.

</details>

**[\`FP107\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp107) optional-forwarded-to-required** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:24:18\`

Required input "notes" of .github/workflows/build.yml is fed from optional input "release-notes" without a default

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** The call looks complete, so GitHub never complains about the required input, but when the outer caller omits the optional value the callee receives an empty string. The "required" guarantee is lost one level up.

**Fix:** Make the outer input required too, give it a default, or add a fallback: \`\${{ inputs.x || 'value' }}\`.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:12:7\` — optional, no default
- \`.github/workflows/build.yml:8:7\` — required by .github/workflows/build.yml

</details>

**[\`FP501\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp501) undefined-env-ref** · \`.github/workflows/publish.yml:34:36\`

env.TARGET_URL is not defined in this scope

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** The \`env\` context only contains variables set by the workflow itself — not runner defaults like \`GITHUB_SHA\`. Reads of anything else evaluate to an empty string.

**Fix:** Define the variable under \`env:\`, write it to \`$GITHUB_ENV\` in an earlier step, or use the matching context (e.g. \`github.sha\`).

</details>

### ℹ️ Info (2)

**[\`FP106\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp106) passthrough-dropped** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:25:7\`

jobs.build passes "verbose" to .github/workflows/build.yml, which never reads it

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** In deep call chains values are often forwarded level by level. When one level stops using an input, every caller above it keeps passing data that is silently dropped.

**Fix:** Stop passing the value here, or make the callee actually use (or forward) it.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/build.yml:11:7\` — declared here, never read

</details>

**[\`FP204\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp204) secrets-inherit** · \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:26:5\`

jobs.build inherits all secrets; .github/workflows/build.yml and its callees read REGISTRY_TOKEN

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Inherit makes the secret flow invisible: nobody can tell from the caller which secrets reach which job, and every nested workflow gets all of them.

**Fix:** Replace with:

\`\`\`yaml
secrets:
  REGISTRY_TOKEN: \${{ secrets.REGISTRY_TOKEN }}
\`\`\`

</details>
"
`;

exports[`renderMarkdown > renders the incident report 1`] = `
"## flowpact report

<sub>flowpact v0.0.0-test · config schema v1 · contract schema v1 · report schema v1 · 7 ms</sub>

❌ **1 error**

| Errors | Warnings | Info | Suppressed | Workflows | Actions | Jobs | Matrix combinations |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 3 | 3 |

### ❌ Errors (1)

**[\`FP401\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp401) empty-binding-for-matrix-combo** · \`.github/workflows/tests.yml:23:19\`

Input "config" for .github/workflows/run-suite.yml is empty in 1 of 3 matrix combinations — matrix.config is not defined there

Matrix: \`{ name: windows }\`

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** GitHub evaluates a missing matrix key to an empty string — no error, no warning. The affected matrix leg runs with an empty input, so the callee may skip its real work (e.g. a test configuration) while the run stays green.

**Fix:** Set \`config\` in every combination, or use a fallback: \`\${{ matrix.config || '<default>' }}\`.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/workflows/pipeline.yml:9:11\` — jobs.tests calls .github/workflows/tests.yml
- \`.github/workflows/tests.yml:18:13\` — this include entry has no \`config\`
- \`.github/workflows/run-suite.yml:11:7\` — receives the empty value: input "config"
- \`.github/workflows/run-suite.yml:17:9\` — this condition reads "config", so the legs with an empty value take the other branch

</details>
"
`;

exports[`renderMarkdown contracts and suppressions > summarizes contract drift with breaking changes 1`] = `
"## flowpact report

<sub>flowpact v0.0.0-test · config schema v1 · contract schema v1 · report schema v1 · 7 ms</sub>

❌ **3 errors**

| Errors | Warnings | Info | Suppressed | Workflows | Actions | Jobs | Matrix combinations |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 3 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 2 | 0 |

### ❌ Errors (3)

**[\`FP803\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp803) breaking-interface-change** · \`.github/workflows/deploy.yml:3:3\`

Breaking change to .github/workflows/deploy.yml: input "region" was removed — callers that pass it will fail

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Callers written against the locked interface will fail (unknown or missing input) or silently read empty outputs. In large pipelines those callers may live in other repositories or rarely-run branches.

**Fix:** Update every caller first (flowpact lists the known consumers), then regenerate the contract. If the change is intended, \`flowpact generate\` records it and the diff makes the break explicit in review.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml:1:1\` — locked contract
- \`.github/workflows/release.yml:5:11\` — consumer: .github/workflows/release.yml › jobs.deploy

</details>

**[\`FP803\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp803) breaking-interface-change** · \`.github/workflows/deploy.yml:8:7\`

Breaking change to .github/workflows/deploy.yml: input "token-scope" was added and must be passed — existing callers do not pass it

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** Callers written against the locked interface will fail (unknown or missing input) or silently read empty outputs. In large pipelines those callers may live in other repositories or rarely-run branches.

**Fix:** Update every caller first (flowpact lists the known consumers), then regenerate the contract. If the change is intended, \`flowpact generate\` records it and the diff makes the break explicit in review.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml:1:1\` — locked contract
- \`.github/workflows/release.yml:5:11\` — consumer: .github/workflows/release.yml › jobs.deploy

</details>

**[\`FP802\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp802) contract-outdated** · \`.github/workflows/deploy.yml:11:7\`

Contract .github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml is outdated: input "legacy" was added

<details><summary>Why / fix</summary>

**Why:** The contract is the reviewed record of what flows in and out. When it drifts silently, the next reviewer compares against stale information.

**Fix:** Run \`flowpact generate\` and commit the updated contracts. In CI, the flowpact action (check mode) attaches the regenerated contracts and a \`git apply\`-able patch to the run — see its job summary.

**Related locations:**

- \`.github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml:1:1\` — locked contract

</details>

### Contracts

❌ Contracts drifted: 0 new · 1 changed · 0 removed · 1 unchanged — **2 breaking changes**

| File | Status | Breaking |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| \`.github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml\` | changed | 2 |

- \`.github/flowpact/contracts/workflows/deploy.contract.yaml\`
  - **input "region" was removed — callers that pass it will fail** (breaking)
  - **input "token-scope" was added and must be passed — existing callers do not pass it** (breaking)
  - input "legacy" was added

Run \`flowpact generate\` and commit the result to update the locked contracts.

<details><summary>1 suppressed finding</summary>

| Code | Location | Reason | Expires | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [\`FP104\`](https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp104) | \`.github/workflows/deploy.yml:11:7\` | Kept for callers on v1 \\| removed in v3 | 2099-01-01 | @​platform |

</details>
"
`;
